# Temperance — V2i onboarding dance (Path A2)
- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: fix/cli-254-v2i-onboarding-dance
- scope-decision: Fix at the shared drive_start layer via opt-in env var.
  One lib edit + one entry.sh wire + 5 Tier 0 tests. No changes to
  per-skill drives or catalog. Backward-compatible (default 0 = no
  behavior change for existing callers).
- drift-trigger: If drive.log after CI run shows Claude still on
  onboarding screens, do NOT crank up the Enter count blindly. Read
  the log; discriminate between "one more gate" vs "wrong keystroke"
  vs "spurious READY match still". File follow-on per finding.

## Checklist
- RIGHT THING? Yes — Path B falsified; the picker needs a keystroke,
  not more settings.json fields.
- SIMPLEST? Yes — bake dance into drive_start; all 3 per-skill drives
  inherit it. Env var default 0 keeps fake_claude tests unchanged.
- BRUTE FORCE? No — diagnosed via real drive.log content (not guessing).
- BLAST RADIUS? Small — only real-claude callers with the env var set
  get the dance. Fake_claude tests default 0. Adopter machines untouched.
- VERIFICATION? Rerun docker-smoke; drives should exit 0 or a
  non-timeout code. If timeout persists, drive.log tells us the next gate.
- REVERSIBLE? Yes — one lib block + one entry.sh export line; delete
  both to revert.
